WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:02.910
People have been dancing since the dawn of
time.

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.070
It's one of the oldest artforms known to man.

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.990
But while dancing can often lighten the mood,
sometimes it can be downright horrific.

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:13.830
While a good guy dance routine can make audiences
smile, a bad guy breakdown is guaranteed to

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.700
send chills through the movie theater.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:19.970
From psychopathic thugs with a love of swing
tunes to disturbed supervillains with a fondness

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:24.850
for hip-hop, these are the creepiest movie
dances of all time.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:26.060
Candy-colored clown

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.770
Almost everything David Lynch has done feels
like a dream.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.010
Blue Velvet is certainly no exception.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:34.760
While it's a little more grounded in reality
than some of his other films, the movie has

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.200
plenty of eerie moments.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:41.670
And when it comes to pure, surreal spookiness,
it doesn't get any creepier than the "In Dreams"

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:42.670
dance sequence.

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:46.620
The otherworldly floor show gets started when
college student Jeffrey Beaumont is abducted

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.890
by a savage gangster named Frank Booth.

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:53.499
Soon, Jeffrey, Frank, and their criminal companions
wind up in the world's weirdest bordello,

00:00:53.499 --> 00:00:55.129
run by a guy named Ben.

00:00:55.129 --> 00:01:00.171
At Frank's request, Ben performs Roy Orbison's
"In Dreams," an eerie song about a candy-colored

00:01:00.171 --> 00:01:01.171
clown.

00:01:01.171 --> 00:01:04.750
The entire sequence is more of a nightmare
than a dream, and it's one dance that you

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.500
won't forget for a long time.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.979
The goblin ball

00:01:08.979 --> 00:01:13.829
Directed by Jim Henson, Labyrinth is a beloved
coming-of-age fantasy, but really, it's about

00:01:13.829 --> 00:01:16.330
a full-grown dude stalking an underage girl.

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:20.500
Okay, it's not really about that, but Jennifer
Connelly being 15 does make the film feel

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:24.140
kind of freaky, as David Bowie was 23 years
her senior.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:27.729
And things get extra weird during the masked
ball sequence.

00:01:27.729 --> 00:01:31.850
After eating an enchanted peach that puts
her to sleep, teenaged Sarah winds up in a

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:35.690
dreamlike party that has some serious Eyes
Wide Shut vibes.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:40.079
Everyone is wearing creepy monster masks,
and the whole thing feels a little too sinister.

00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:44.140
It gets even weirder when Jareth the Goblin
King makes his move, seducing the girl with

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:47.409
his '80s hair, waltzing prowess, and tight
pants.

00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:51.040
Fortunately, when Sarah realizes it's all
a distraction to stop her from saving her

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:56.640
brother, she snaps out of her spell and makes
a grand exit, literally crashing the party.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:57.640
Buffalo Bill boogie

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:02.619
The morbid world of Thomas Harris is populated
with all sorts of serial killers, but none

00:02:02.619 --> 00:02:07.659
of these psychos have moves like Jame Gumb,
aka Buffalo Bill, in The Silence of the Lambs.

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:11.870
During his infamous dance scene, Buffalo Bill
is down in his basement and totally oblivious

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:14.350
to the screaming woman he's stashed away in
his dungeon.

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:17.980
Listening to "Goodbye Horses," Bill sashays
around the room, wearing nothing more than

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:20.040
a robe, stockings, and a woman's scalp.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.530
In an interview with Rolling Stone, Levine
said he'd originally prepared a stripper routine,

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:27.140
but ended up going with more of a David Bowie
glam vibe.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:30.120
Honestly, it would have been creepy either
way.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.400
Stuck in the middle

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.260
Mr. Blonde is many things.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:37.900
He's a thief, an ex-con, a murderer, and a
sadist, and to top it all off, the man fancies

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:39.670
himself something of a performer.

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:44.010
The nastiest thug in Reservoir Dogs, Blonde
gets way too much pleasure torturing a poor

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.010
police officer.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:49.379
"I don't really give a good f—- what you
know or don't know.

00:02:49.379 --> 00:02:52.590
But I'm gonna torture you anyway."

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:56.420
It's a horrific scene, even if the worst part
does happen off-screen, but what makes it

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:00.100
worse is how Blonde is strutting around the
warehouse, grooving to Stealers Wheel and

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.410
taking his sweet time before getting busy.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:07.120
His twisted little dance draws out the tension
as long as possible before the bloodshed begins.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.760
As far as movie dances go, this is easily
one of the most painful to watch.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.430
Black Swan takeover

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:18.060
Sometimes becoming a great artist means working
for untold hours until you one day achieve

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.060
perfection.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:22.700
And sometimes it means you're haunted by doppelgangers,
and you start morphing into a bird.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.720
At least, that's what happens to Nina Sayers
in Black Swan.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.300
"It's my turn!"

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:36.760
A naive ballerina struggling to keep the lead
role in Swan Lake, Nina falls deeper and deeper

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:38.580
into madness over the course of the film.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:42.940
But when she finally gives in to the darkness,
she delivers the performance of her life.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:55.020
And while this creepy dance eventually climaxes
with disastrous results, Natalie Portman danced

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:58.400
away from it all with an Oscar for best actress.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.290
Dance ex machina

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:04.790
Everything about Ex Machina is unsettling,
from the isolated landscape to Alicia Vikander's

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:05.930
chilling performance.

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:09.810
It's an unbearably tense movie, and it never
lets up, even when the sense of dread gives

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:12.439
way to one of the greatest dance scenes in
cinema history.

00:04:12.439 --> 00:04:17.380
The sci-fi disco gets started after a computer
programmer named Caleb is chosen by billionaire

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:21.030
inventor Nathan to help test whether robot
Ava can pass for human.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:25.280
However, things start getting creepy very
quickly, and soon, Caleb suspects Nathan's

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.770
relationship with his robot Ava might be a
tad unhealthy.

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:32.820
But when Caleb goes to confront Nathan about
his obsessive behavior, the tech genius ignores

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:36.290
Caleb's questions and starts to boogie beside
his mistress, Kyoko.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:42.440
"However you would not be wasting your time
if you were dancing with her."

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:48.960
Their choreography is a little too perfect,
and this out-of-nowhere number will give you

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:53.750
the creeps even before you find out the secret
to their musical success.

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:55.240
Hedwig busts a move

00:04:55.240 --> 00:05:00.210
Anya Taylor-Joy is fantastic in Split, but
it's James McAvoy who's constantly stealing

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:01.210
the show.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:06.500
McAvoy plays Kevin Wendell Crumb, a man with
23 different personalities, including a 9-year-old

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:07.800
boy named Hedwig.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:12.710
But Hedwig isn't pure evil; he's just a scared,
confused kid who wants to show Casey his CD

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:13.710
player.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:18.120
Sensing an opportunity to escape Kevin's dungeon,
Casey takes Hedwig up on his offer but winds

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.740
up witnessing one of the scariest moments
in the movie.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:24.830
On the one hand, watching McAvoy dance with
such enthusiasm is pretty entertaining.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.800
At the same time, Hedwig's dance is downright
disturbing.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:32.410
We're watching a truly sick man here, a guy
grooving to hip-hop music while he's got several

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:34.710
girls locked away in his own private prison.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:38.800
The look on Anya Taylor-Joy's face really
sums it up: the perfect mix of horror and

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:39.800
bewilderment.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:40.800
"Wow"

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:41.940
"I know."

